Subject: [PATCH] a warlock life taps only from a health floor it can fight from

WHY THIS PATCH EXISTS

On the dev realm the natural guilds' warlocks are caught in death loops far
more than any other class. Measured over one day (overseer_death and the
module's "guild death" log lines, members at levels 40 to 49):

  * warlocks died about 60 times a day each; every other class about 32;
  * 23 of the 36 members in a death loop were warlocks;
  * the warlocks died to LOWER level creatures than the other classes did
    (killer level minus member level averaged -1.4 against -0.6, and 21% of
    warlock deaths were to a creature five or more levels below them).

Dying to easy creatures says the warlock starts its fights hurt. This tree
makes it do so:

  * LifeTapTrigger (src/Ai/Class/Warlock/WarlockTriggers.cpp) fires whenever
    mana is below 85% and health is above Playerbots.LowHealth (45 by
    default). GenericWarlockNonCombatStrategy wires it to "life tap" at 23,
    out of combat, and each spec's combat strategy wires it again as a
    filler at 5.1.
  * The food strategy eats only on "low health" (UseFoodStrategy.cpp), the
    same 45, because the realm runs with the food cheat off on purpose.

So between pulls a warlock taps its health down to just above 45%, which is
exactly where eating would start and never does, and walks into the next
fight at half health. Every cast that costs mana re-arms the tap. Of the
guild members whose saved health is below full, warlocks are 18 of 52, the
other classes together 12 of 107.

WHAT IT CHANGES

The trigger's floor: almost full health (Playerbots.AlmostFullHealth, 85)
out of combat, medium health (Playerbots.MediumHealth, 65) in combat. Out of
combat a warlock now taps only from near full health and then lets its
health come back before tapping again; in combat the filler tap stops at
65% instead of 45%.

WHAT IT DELIBERATELY DOES NOT CHANGE

  * The emergency tap. GenericWarlockStrategy wires "low mana" to "life tap"
    at 95, and CastLifeTapAction::isUseful keeps its own low-health check.
    A warlock out of mana in a fight still taps down to 45%.
  * The thresholds themselves, which every class reads.
  * Which pet a warlock summons. 25 of the guilds' 51 warlocks at 30 to 55
    never learned Summon Voidwalker (a class quest reward) and fight with
    the Imp; that is a class-quest question, not this trigger's.

WHEN THIS PATCH SHOULD BE DELETED. When upstream gives LifeTapTrigger a
floor above low health. apply-patches.sh fails the build the day the
context lines change, which is the intended way to find out.

diff --git a/src/Ai/Class/Warlock/WarlockTriggers.cpp b/src/Ai/Class/Warlock/WarlockTriggers.cpp
index e0e0f39..49166da 100644
--- a/src/Ai/Class/Warlock/WarlockTriggers.cpp
+++ b/src/Ai/Class/Warlock/WarlockTriggers.cpp
@@ -90,10 +90,15 @@ bool DecimationTrigger::IsActive()
     return aura && aura->GetDuration() > 3000;
 }
 
-// Checks if the bot's mana is below 85% and health is above a low health threshold
+// Checks if the bot's mana is below 85% and health is at least a floor: medium
+// health in combat, almost full health out of combat. Eating starts only below
+// low health, so a floor at low health kept a warlock near half health between
+// pulls, and it opened every fight there.
 bool LifeTapTrigger::IsActive()
 {
-    if (AI_VALUE2(uint8, "health", "self target") <= sPlayerbotAIConfig.LowHealth)
+    uint32 const healthFloor =
+        bot->IsInCombat() ? sPlayerbotAIConfig.MediumHealth : sPlayerbotAIConfig.AlmostFullHealth;
+    if (AI_VALUE2(uint8, "health", "self target") < healthFloor)
         return false;
 
     if (!AI_VALUE2(bool, "has mana", "self target"))
